From: Uke Linux project <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: report the Uke SM7675 SoC through cpuinfo Hardware

Original Fastfetch reads Hardware on ARM before its DT-compatible fallback.
Expose the actual SoC name only for Uke/SM7675, without changing MIDR, core
identity, topology or frequency reporting. Original Solid continues to
identify individual CPU cores from implementer and part IDs.

--- a/arch/arm64/kernel/cpuinfo.c
+++ b/arch/arm64/kernel/cpuinfo.c
@@ -17,6 +17,7 @@
 #include <linux/elf.h>
 #include <linux/init.h>
 #include <linux/kernel.h>
+#include <linux/of.h>
 #include <linux/personality.h>
 #include <linux/preempt.h>
 #include <linux/printk.h>
@@ -237,6 +238,10 @@
 		seq_printf(m, "model name\t: ARMv8 Processor rev %d (%s)\n",
 			   MIDR_REVISION(midr), COMPAT_ELF_PLATFORM);
 
+	if (of_machine_is_compatible("xiaomi,uke") &&
+	    of_machine_is_compatible("qcom,sm7675"))
+		seq_puts(m, "Hardware\t: Qualcomm Snapdragon 7+ Gen 3 (SM7675)\n");
+
 	seq_printf(m, "BogoMIPS\t: %lu.%02lu\n",
 		   loops_per_jiffy / (500000UL/HZ),
 		   loops_per_jiffy / (5000UL/HZ) % 100);
